gaussian_filtered_image = imfilter(gray_image, gaussian_filter);
% Define Sobel operator in x direction
sobel_x = [-1 0 1; -2 0 2; -1 0 1];
% Define Sobel operator in y direction
sobel_y = [-1 -2 -1; 0 0 0; 1 2 1];
% Apply Sobel operator in x direction
edge_image_x = conv2(double(gaussian_filtered_image), sobel_x, 'same');
% Apply Sobel operator in y direction
edge_image_y = conv2(double(gaussian_filtered_image), sobel_y, 'same');
% Combine edges in both directions
edge_image = sqrt(edge_image_x.^2 + edge_image_y.^2);
% Display original image and edge image
subplot(1, 2, 1), imshow(input_image), title('Original Image');
subplot(1, 2, 2), imshow(edge_image), title('Edge Image');
```
This code applies a Gaussian filter using the `fspecial` function to create a 3x3 filter with a standard deviation of 0.5. Then it filters the grayscale image using the `imfilter` function. Afterward, the Sobel edge detection is applied as usual on the filtered image. The resulting edge image is displayed alongside the original image for comparison.

