 Hello! I'd be happy to help you create a PHP custom function called `smart_sort_array`. Here's how you can implement it based on your requirements:

```php
function smart_sort_array($set, $order = 'ASC') {
    $size = count($set);
    for ($i = 0; $i < $size - 1; $i++) {
        for ($j = $i + 1; $j < $size; $j++) {
            if (($order == 'ASC' && $set[$i]['age'] > $set[$j]['age']) || ($order == 'DESC' && $set[$i]['age'] < $set[$j]['age'])) {
                // Swap elements i and j by referencing
                $temp = $set[$i];
                $set[$i] = $set[$j];
                $set[$j] = $temp;
            }
        }
    }
    return $set;
}
```

This function accepts two parameters: `$set` which is an associative array containing other associative arrays as elements, and `$order` which is an optional parameter that defaults to 'ASC' for ascending order or 'DESC' for descending order. The function uses a nested loop to compare adjacent elements in the array based on their age values and swaps them accordingly using a temporary variable. After sorting, the function returns the sorted array.

You can test the function with some sample data like this:

```php
