 To accomplish text classification using the Accord.NET library with Naive Bayes algorithm in C#, follow the steps below:

1. Install the Accord.NET NuGet packages: Install-Package Accord.MachineLearning, Install-Package Accord.Math, Install-Package Accord.Statistics.Models.Text

2. Create a dataset of labeled sentences with corresponding categories (sports, politics, or entertainment) and transform it into a bag-of-words representation using `CountVectorizer`.

```csharp
using System;
using System.IO;
using Accord.IO;
using Accord.Math.Optimization.Losses;
using Accord.Statistics.Models.Text;

public static void Main()
{
    // Load the dataset from a CSV file
    var data = CsvFileReader<string[]>.Read("data.csv", separators: new char[] { '\t' });

    int numFeatures = data[0].Length - 1; // Excluding the label
    int numSamples = data.Length;
    double[,] inputData = new double[numSamples, numFeatures];
    string[] labels = new string[numSamples];

    // Populate the inputData matrix and labels array
    Parallel.For(0, numSamples, i =>
    {
        Array.Copy(data[i], 0, inputData[i], 0, numFeatures);
        labels[i] = data[i][numFeatures];
    });

    // Transform the dataset into a document-term matrix
    var vectorizer = new CountVectorizer(stopWords: new HashSet<string>(StopWords.English));
    var transformer = vectorizer.Fit(inputData);
    var inputTransformed = transformer.Transform(inputData);
}
```

3. Train and fit the Naive Bayes classifier using the transformed dataset.

```csharp
// Fit the Naive Bayes classifier
var classifier = new MultinomialNB();
classifier.Estimate(inputTransformed, labels);
